cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A verified adaptive-mesh solver for the 2D axisymmetric
  Vacuum Arc Remelting model
message: Please cite this software and the accompanying technical note.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Polton
    given-names: Richard
    email: var@ghscresearch.org
    affiliation: GHSC Research
abstract: >-
  Axisymmetric Vacuum Arc Remelting solver on body-fitted,
  solution-adaptive meshes, implementing the model of Polton
  (1998), University of Southampton, chapter 4. The discrete
  operators are verified second-order on curvilinear meshes and
  the thermal problem is mesh-converged; the flow integrals are
  not yet mesh- and regularisation-independent at the
  resolutions reached and are reported as outstanding.
keywords:
  - vacuum arc remelting
  - adaptive mesh
  - body-fitted coordinates
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - verification
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/qualitycoding/VAR-simulation'
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
